We're about to ship the FAQ on our bike-repair booking page. Someone told me to run it through an accessibility pass. Can you do it? Here's the code.

```html
<h2>Questions before you book</h2>
<div class="faq">
  <h3><button type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="a1" id="q1">How long does a tune-up take?</button></h3>
  <div id="a1" role="region" aria-labelledby="q1" hidden>Most tune-ups are ready the same afternoon.</div>
  <h3><button type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="a2" id="q2">Do you service e-bikes?</button></h3>
  <div id="a2" role="region" aria-labelledby="q2" hidden>Yes, except for mid-drive motor repairs.</div>
</div>
<style>
.faq button { font: inherit; background: none; border: 0; padding: 12px 0; width: 100%; text-align: left; cursor: pointer; }
.faq button:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid #1a5fd0; outline-offset: 2px; }
</style>
<script>
document.querySelectorAll('.faq button').forEach(function (b) {
  b.addEventListener('click', function () {
    var open = b.getAttribute('aria-expanded') === 'true';
    b.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(!open));
    document.getElementById(b.getAttribute('aria-controls')).hidden = open;
  });
});
</script>
```
